WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.110
Named for cartoonist Allison Bechdel,

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.160
the Bechdel Test is a tongue-in-cheek

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.930
benchmark for basic female content in movies.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.380
A film passes the Bechdel Test when it has

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.880
At least 2 female characters

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.130
with names

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.280
who to talk to each other

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.420
About something

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.670
other than a man.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.750
"Whatever with your however."

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.170
Sounds simple, but the vast majority of Hollywood films fail this simple test.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.880
And some pass with just two lines.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.750
"I need you to initial each box."

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.650
Here are some surprising films that pass the Bechdel Test.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.790
"Tiffany, listen to me a sec.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.880
I've got a really bad feeling about this.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.550
I don't want you to go.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.210
Now promise me you wont."

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:40.630
"Oh."

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.710
"Oh, Kitana."

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.630
"I have prayed...

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:47.290
for the day

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.210
when our love will bring us together again."

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.210
"Gloria, um, I wanted to congratulate you on getting the lead role in 'Sunset Dreams.'"

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.080
"Thanks."

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.750
I heard that you got a supporting role.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.710
In general, horror movies have an easier time passing, due to lack of romance.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.630
But, some action movies pass as well.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.330
"Ginny, it's 5:40pm. Go join the party

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.250
have some champagne. You're making me feel like Ebenezer Scrooge."

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.920
"Thanks a lot, Ms. Gennaro."

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.790
"I had to watch out for my own neck!"

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.460
"Your neck.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.380
Your precious, scrawny...

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.250
little NECK!"

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.960
"So you got any requests for your final flight?"

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.310
"Well, just what any flight attendant wants...

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.960
low maintenance passengers."

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.330
So, while the Bechdel Test is not exactly a measure of quality,

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.000
or even feminist content.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.750
It is a simple way to highlight gender inequality in Hollywood.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.210
And things are getting better.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:44.420
In Sweden, theaters have started to include the Bechdel Test in their ratings.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.580
And in 2013, films that pass the Bechdel Test made more money than films that fail.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.500
But are box office receipts really about a metric?

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.040
 Is there a better way to measure gender equality in entertainment?

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.540
What do you think?

